==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Succubus Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Queen Succubus Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Lilith Cat is the Halloween variant of [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Cat]], having a high chance to freeze [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies rather than [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]. Similar to Ice Cat, she has a relatively fast recharge time and cheap cost for an uber, which may allow her to stack on certain stages. When stacked, she is a reliable neutraliser for melee Angels such as [[Boraphim]], [[Divine Cyclone]], hordes of [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] and also [[Cala Maria]], if meatshielded sufficiently. Her health and damage, however, leave much to be desired, not only making her highly impractical in stages without Angels as a threat, but also making her vulnerable to rushes from melee Angels and long-ranged enemies like [[Sunfish Jones]]. In terms of crowd-control, 375 isn't a bad range against Angels, outranging [[Winged Pigge]]'s Omni Strike and even [[Angelic Sleipnir]], but her long foreswing and 25% chance not to freeze cause her to sometimes allow unfrozen Angels to push and destroy her. In practice, she also performs poorly against Sleipnir, as she only outranges him by 3 range and tends to clip into his range; similarly, if Winged Pigge is with other pushers like [[R.Ost]] such as in [[Heaven's Oasis]], Lilith is left utterly useless due the rapid-pushing and lack of health. Overall, a usable unit in niche and irrelevant outside of referred use. Even against units she counters well, she tends to be outperformed by [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and sometimes [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
Queen Succubus Cat only gains a slight damage boost, 10 range and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies as targets. Against Angels, the only notable change is that she can now counter Angelic Sleipnir more reliably, but that's pretty much it. None of her other issues are fixed and the better damage is still very far from enough to make her worth bringing along for anything but her freeze.

When put against Aku enemies, Queen Succubus still tends to be a bad pick, especially since far superior alternatives tend to be available. Since [[Shield]]s block status effects, she can only be theoretically useful against threats without Shields, such as [[Aku Gory]] and [[Condemned Peng]], and has to rely on [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing support]] in order to be borderline useful, provided if she hasn't been nuked by [[Surge Attack|Surges]] already. Even if she gets the chance, it still proves inconsistent since most [[:Category:Enemies with Shields|Shielded enemies]] outrange her, not to mention some can recover their Shields easily to deny her ability, completely removing what little effectiveness she had.

==='''Talents'''===
Queen Succubus Cat gains a decent amount of improvements through Talents, but not enough to offset her poor standing in the meta prior to these improvements.

'''[[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Wave]]''' is a genuinely good addition, granting Succubus pierce that extends her effective reach up to 533 range, while applying Freeze to any targets hit. She does need to actually hit an enemy for it to apply, however, and it barely does anything for her DPS either. This is easily her best Talent, but it comes at quite the NP cost which may not be worth it if any alternative [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control options]] are available.

'''[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]]''' is a more straightforward upgrade, patching up her weakness to Death Surges, as well as [[Medu-san]]. It also enables better usage against [[St. Dober]] and [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] for her Angel matchups. Her usage as a general Anti-Surge is still far from ideal due to her low stats.

Lastly is [[Immune to Freeze]], which doesn't do much in the context of Aku/Angel, although it does improve performance against [[Wicked Face]] and [[Chickful A]]. This is mainly useful in mixed stages with [[Henry]], which are few and far between, since most other [[:Category:Enemies with Freeze ability|Freezing enemies]] would eradicate her instantly if she doesn't inherently outrange them.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' are what you would expect, but neither is a worthwhile improvement to Queen Succubus Cat. She is first and foremost a crowd-controller, one who relies on outranging enemies to make up the bulk of her survivability. This means Defense Buff is rather useless on her. Her damage is equally unimpressive, though with Mini-Wave and Attack Buff in tandem, she does barely get a pass on that front. Regardless, save your NP for something else.

